We are now in DOGFOOD / BUGFIX mode.

Do NOT add new features, commands, models, abstractions, integrations, or architecture.

The current Work → Search → Summary → Report implementation exists, but the real CLI dogfood is failing.

Fix the observed failures and prove the existing milestone end-to-end.

## P0 — Normalize datetime semantics

Observed failures:

```text
TypeError: can't compare offset-naive and offset-aware datetimes
```

This occurs through:

```text
work_service.collect_work_items()
→ items.sort(key=lambda item: item.timestamp, reverse=True)
```

and affects:

```bash
conciencia work summarize --since 2026-08-27
conciencia ask "Resumime todo lo que desarrollé desde el 27 de agosto hasta hoy"
conciencia work search "WebMCP"
```

Do NOT patch only the `.sort()` line.

Audit all timestamp sources used by Work:

* database activities
* missions
* mission runs
* signals
* evidence
* deliverables/reports
* Git commits
* since/until parsing
* datetime.utcnow()/now()
* SQLAlchemy values

Define ONE internal datetime policy.

Preferred:

```text
timezone-aware UTC internally
```

Normalize every WorkItem timestamp at the ingestion boundary.

Also normalize `since` and `until`.

Do not compare mixed datetime semantics anywhere.

Add regression tests containing BOTH:

```text
naive datetime
aware datetime
```

and verify sorting/filtering works deterministically.

---

## P0 — Fix Report project UUID boundary

Observed:

```text
AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'hex'
```

during:

```bash
conciencia report create --project Conciencia
```

The resolved project identifier is reaching a SQLAlchemy UUID comparison as a string.

Audit:

```text
CLI project resolver
→ report_create
→ summarize_work
→ collect_work_items
→ SQLAlchemy filters
```

Establish a clear identifier boundary.

If database models use UUID objects, convert/validate once before DB filtering.

Do not scatter ad-hoc `UUID(...)` conversions throughout the codebase.

Reuse the existing Project resolution service/helper where possible.

Test:

```bash
conciencia report create --project Conciencia
conciencia report create --project <UUID>
```

Both should resolve to the same project.

---

## P1 — Validate project scoping

The current WorkItems show many historical records with:

```text
project_id=None
```

while the current workspace knows the active Conciencia project.

Do NOT silently assign old records to Conciencia.

Instead verify and document current semantics:

```text
project_id present
→ project-scoped evidence

project_id absent
→ workspace-level/unscoped historical evidence
```

For:

```bash
conciencia work summarize --since 2026-08-27
```

when run from the Conciencia repository, decide explicitly whether the default means:

A. current project only

or

B. workspace-wide history with current project context

Use the product model consistently.

Recommended:

```text
conciencia work ...
→ workspace-wide by default

conciencia work ... --project current
→ current project

conciencia work ... --project Conciencia
→ explicit project
```

Do not lose unscoped historical evidence.

